/connectivity\/blockcuttree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The block–cut tree of an undirected graph (Harary’s block-cutpoint tree, JGraphT’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BlockCutpointGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"): a node per block and per articulation point, and an edge joining each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"block to each articulation point it contains. Blocks are numbered as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blocks"},{"type":"text","text":", articulation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"points by their place in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"articulationPoints"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order). It is a forest: one tree per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected component with an edge that is not a self-loop; isolated vertices are no node."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BlockCutTree","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"}}}